Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?uhf-sdk:=20add=20the=20Phase=204=20developer=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?SDK=20(SRS=20=C2=A77),=20compiled=20and=20tested=20for=20real?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements UHF-SRS-001 §7 SDK-01/03/04/06/07/08/09: a thin Kotlin/Java
facade over android.hardware.uhf.UhfManager, distributed as
com.rockchip.uhf:uhf-sdk. Unlike most of this patch series, this layer
was not just written and cross-checked by hand — a real toolchain turned
up in this environment (prebuilts/build-tools aidl,
prebuilts/sdk/34/system/android.jar, external/kotlinc, JUnit) and was
used to actually compile and, where possible, run every file added here.

- UhfSdkSession/RealUhfSdkSession/UhfSdk (SDK-01/03/04): the session
  interface mirrors android.hardware.uhf.UhfSession method-for-method;
  RealUhfSdkSession is pure 1:1 delegation, verified by compiling it
  directly against the real compiled UhfSession class rather than a
  hand-written stub standing in for it.

- FakeUhfSdkSession (SDK-09): an in-memory reader enforcing the same
  contracts the platform arbiter does (FR-SEC-02 kill-password check,
  FR-SEC-04 permanent-lock confirmation, FR-MEM-06 word-range validation)
  so code passing against the fake has already met what a real reader
  would also demand. FakeUhfSdkSessionTest's 12 tests were compiled and
  actually executed against JUnit 4 (not just compiled), including
  exercising real background streaming via a genuine
  ScheduledExecutorService. All pass.

- UhfSdkKt.kt (SDK-08): coroutine/Flow adapters, compiled with a real
  Kotlin 1.8.10 compiler against a real kotlinx-coroutines-core jar.
  inventorySuspend() is deliberately not named inventory() — verified
  empirically (not assumed) that a same-named suspend extension compiles
  but is silently shadowed by UhfSdkSession's existing blocking member
  and becomes unreachable through ordinary call syntax.

- sdk/sample/ (SDK-05): a reference app demonstrating every API group in
  the order SRS §7's own usage example presents them; also compiled for
  real against the same classpath.

A real, incidental bug in the platform layer (frameworks/base, not this
commit) was caught by this verification effort and fixed separately:
IUhfService.aidl needs a companion <ClassName>.aidl declaration for every
custom Parcelable it references. Missing since Phase 1; found by actually
running the aidl compiler for the first time in this series.

STATUS: no Gradle/AGP build was performed (unavailable in this
environment) — packaging into an AAR, resource/manifest merging, and any
device or emulator run remain untested. SDK-02's stub jar (generated from
the platform API signature files via metalava) does not exist yet; this
verification used the real compiled platform classes directly instead,
which proves the SDK source is correct against the real API shape without
that specific packaged artifact. SDK-10 (Maven publishing) not attempted.
See uhf-sdk/README.md for the full verified-vs-not breakdown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
